--- task
id: a05
dataset: attribution
kind: delete nodes selected by an anti-join
answer: fewest
composition: a write fed by a read: the touchpoints to delete are known only through their source's neighbours, so edition 2 reads their slugs and deletes by key

--- intent
Delete every touchpoint that landed on a source no channel watches.

--- edition2
query unwatched() {
  match { $t: Touchpoint  $t touchpointOnSource $s  not { $c channelWatchesSource $s } }
  return { $t.slug }
}

--- edition2 bind ids=1:t.slug
query drop_unwatched($ids: [String]) {
  delete Touchpoint where slug in $ids
}

--- edition3
query drop_unwatched() {
  $t: Touchpoint
  $t touchpointOnSource $s
  not { $c channelWatchesSource $s }
  delete $t
}

--- check
query check() {
  match { $t: Touchpoint }
  return { $t.slug }
}

--- expect unordered
columns: ["t.slug"]
["t1"]
["t3"]
["t4"]
["t5"]
["t8"]
["t10"]
